*

# --- Dockerfile (x86_64 cross-compilation image) ---
!Ascend-cann-toolkit_*_linux-x86_64.run
!Ascend-cann-toolkit_*_linux-aarch64.run
!torch-*-cp310-cp310-manylinux_2_28_aarch64.whl
!assemble_sysroot.sh
!verify.sh

# --- Dockerfile.aarch64 (native AArch64 offline inference image) ---
# deps/ carries the whole offline payload: the CANN .run, the AArch64
# wheelhouse, the local apt archive and the vllm-ascend source. It is
# bind-mounted at build time, never COPYed, so it costs no image layer.
!deps
# ...but not the parts Dockerfile.aarch64 never reads. The vLLM source is only
# needed while provisioning builds its wheel, and .provision is scratch space.
deps/src/vllm
deps/.provision

# Bind-mounted by Dockerfile.aarch64, so they must stay in the context.
!packages.aarch64.txt
!requirements.aarch64.txt
!constraints.aarch64.txt

# COPYed into the image.
!entrypoint.sh
!verify_runtime.sh
